From: Surendra Singh Chouhan <kr494167@gmail.com>

sky1_reset_assert(), sky1_reset_deassert(), sky1_reset(), and
sky1_reset_status() ignored the return values of sky1_reset_set() and
regmap_read(). If regmap operations failed (e.g. due to bus I/O errors),
error codes were swallowed and functions returned success (0) or incorrect
status (1).

In addition, sky1_src_signals is a sparse array containing unmapped entries
(offset == 0 && bit == 0). Out-of-bounds id lookups or references to
unmapped entries were not validated before performing regmap operations.

Fix these by capturing and propagating regmap read/write errors across
all ops, and adding bounds and unmapped signal validation in
sky1_reset_set() and sky1_reset_status().

Fixes: 7cd3ca90d921 ("reset: add Sky1 soc reset support")
